# Copy this file to .env and adjust as needed for local development.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real secrets here. In staging/prod,
# these are injected as real environment variables, not a file (main.go's
# godotenv.Load() silently no-ops when .env doesn't exist).

# Postgres connection string for the remote Supabase database (there is no
# local Postgres in docker-compose.yml). Use the connection string from the
# Supabase dashboard (Project Settings > Database); sslmode=require.
#
# cmd/server (the API) connects as slbus_app — a non-superuser role
# (db/migrations/000005_app_role.up.sql) — because Postgres superusers
# bypass Row-Level Security unconditionally, and the tenant-isolation
# policies in DATABASE_DESIGN.md §5 depend on the connection NOT being a
# superuser. Do not point the API at the slbus superuser account.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://slbus_app:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# cmd/worker currently runs no RLS-protected queries yet (Phase 3/4 TODOs
# in cmd/worker/main.go), so it can stay on the slbus superuser for now —
# revisit once it does.
# WORKER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://slbus:<password>@<host>:5432/postgres?sslmode=require

# HMAC secret used to sign/verify access tokens (AUTHENTICATION_DESIGN.md
# §4). Generate a real one for anything beyond a throwaway local
# database: `openssl rand -base64 48`.
JWT_SIGNING_KEY=change-me-generate-a-real-secret-with-openssl-rand--base64-48

# Address the HTTP server listens on.
HTTP_ADDR=:8080

# "development" permits the insecure built-in fallbacks for JWT_SIGNING_KEY and
# QR_TOKEN_SECRET. Leave unset (or any other value) in staging/prod: the server
# then refuses to start unless both secrets are provided.
APP_ENV=development

# HMAC secret for booking QR tickets. Generate: `openssl rand -base64 48`.
# QR_TOKEN_SECRET=

# First-run platform admin. If both are set and no platform_admin exists yet,
# the server creates one at startup (no-op afterwards, safe to leave set — but
# remove the password once you've logged in and enrolled MFA). Password must be
# at least 10 characters.
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- Production deploy (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) ---
# These are GitHub Actions secrets; the workflow writes the server's .env from
# them. HTTP_ADDR and REDIS_ADDR are set in deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml.
# DOMAIN=api.example.com            # Caddy gets the HTTPS cert for this
# Production runs its own Postgres container (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml),
# which builds DATABASE_URL / WORKER_DATABASE_URL from these two. URL-safe
# values only: openssl rand -hex 24
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=                # superuser `slbus` (migrations, worker)
# SLBUS_APP_PASSWORD=               # non-superuser `slbus_app` (API)

# Browser origins allowed to call the API (the operator web app). Comma-separated;
# "*" allows any origin (local dev only). Unset = CORS disabled.
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://operator.example.com

# Reverse proxies in front of the API that append to X-Forwarded-For. Per-IP
# rate limits use the right-most entry past this many hops. 0 (default, dev) =
# ignore the header and use the TCP peer. Set 1 behind Caddy (prod sets this in
# deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml). Never set it higher than the real number of
# proxies, or clients can spoof their IP.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=0

# --- Database backups (db-backup service, deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml) ---
# Nightly pg_dump -Fc into the server's db_backups volume. Defaults shown;
# set in the server .env to change. Runbook: runbooks/database-backup-restore.md
# BACKUP_TIME=02:30                 # HH:MM, in BACKUP_TZ
# BACKUP_TZ=Asia/Colombo
# BACKUP_KEEP=14                    # newest N dumps kept, older pruned
# Optional off-site copy, OFF unless BACKUP_S3_BUCKET is set (GitHub secrets of
# the same names). Any S3-compatible store: AWS S3, Backblaze B2, Cloudflare R2.
# Use a key that can only write to this bucket; set retention with a bucket
# lifecycle rule (the script never deletes remote copies).
# BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=               # e.g. https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com,
#                                   # https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com;
#                                   # blank = AWS S3
# BACKUP_S3_REGION=                 # AWS needs it (e.g. ap-south-1); R2: auto
# BACKUP_S3_PREFIX=slbus/           # optional key prefix
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# SMSlenz (SMS OTP second factor) — https://www.smslenz.lk/developers/api
SMSLENZ_BASE_URL=https://www.smslenz.lk/api
SMSLENZ_USER_ID=
SMSLENZ_API_KEY=
SMSLENZ_SENDER_ID=SMSlenzDEMO
# 32+ random bytes, hex: openssl rand -hex 32
OTP_HMAC_KEY=
# Worker alerts when SMSlenz credit falls below this (LKR)
SMS_LOW_BALANCE_ALERT_LKR=500
# Price per SMS segment, for the admin dashboard estimate (LKR)
SMS_UNIT_PRICE_LKR=0.59
